---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" activePage="">
<style>
  .privacy-section {
    padding: 80px 3rem 120px;
    background: var(--white);
  }

  .privacy-body {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .privacy-body h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--espresso);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .privacy-body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .privacy-body p {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    line-height: 1.9;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .privacy-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .privacy-section { padding: 60px 1.5rem 80px; }
  }
</style>

<div class="page-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-label">Legal</div>
  <h1 class="page-hero-title"><strong>Privacy</strong> Policy</h1>
</div>

<section class="privacy-section">
  <div class="privacy-body">

    <p>
      This privacy policy describes how Collabria, Inc. ("Collabria") collects, uses and shares
      information about you when you use our website. Collabria is committed to protecting your
      personal information and your right to privacy.
    </p>

    <h2>Our Core Principles</h2>
    <p>
      We are committed to the responsible collection and use of personal information. As a result,
      we adhere to the following principles:
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not request more personal information than necessary. We do not share your personal
      information with others except as described in this policy, to comply with the law, or to
      develop and improve our products and services. We do not store personal information on our
      servers unless required for the ongoing operation of our services.
    </p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      Like most website operators, Collabria collects non-personally-identifying information of the
      sort that web browsers and servers typically make available, such as the browser type,
      language preference, referring site, and the date and time of each visitor request. Our purpose
      in collecting this information is to better understand how visitors use the website.
    </p>
    <p>
      Collabria also collects potentially personally-identifying information like Internet Protocol
      (IP) addresses. We do not use such information to identify visitors, and do not disclose such
      information other than as described below.
    </p>
    <p>
      Certain visitors to Collabria's website choose to interact with the site in ways that require
      us to gather personally-identifying information. The amount and type of information gathered
      depends on the nature of the interaction. For example, we ask visitors who wish to receive
      updates to provide a name and email address.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing of Information</h2>
    <p>
      We do not disclose personally-identifying information other than as described below.
    </p>
    <p>
      Collabria discloses potentially personally-identifying and personally-identifying information
      only to those of its employees, contractors and affiliated organizations that (i) need to know
      that information in order to process it on Collabria's behalf or to provide services available
      at the website, and (ii) have agreed not to disclose it to others.
    </p>
    <p>
      Collabria will not rent or sell potentially personally-identifying and personally-identifying
      information to anyone. Other than to its employees, contractors and affiliated organizations,
      as described above, Collabria discloses such information only in response to a subpoena, court
      order or other governmental request, or when Collabria believes in good faith that disclosure
      is reasonably necessary to protect the property or rights of Collabria, third parties or the
      public at large.
    </p>

    <h2>Protection of Information</h2>
    <p>
      Collabria takes all measures reasonably necessary to protect against the unauthorized access,
      use, alteration or destruction of potentially personally-identifying and personally-identifying
      information.
    </p>
    <p>
      Collabria's employees, contractors and affiliated organizations that handle personally
      identifying information may be located outside of your home country. By using Collabria's
      website, you consent to the transfer of such information to them.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      A cookie is a string of information that a website stores on a visitor's computer, and that
      the visitor's browser provides to the website each time the visitor returns. Collabria uses
      cookies to help identify and track visitors, their usage of the website, and their website
      access preferences. Visitors who do not wish to have cookies placed on their computers should
      set their browsers to refuse cookies before using the Collabria website.
    </p>
    <p>
      Certain pages of our website may include advertising served by third parties. These companies
      may use cookies to serve ads based on prior visits to our website. This privacy policy does
      not apply to, and we cannot control the activities of, these other advertisers.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      Collabria reserves the right to change this privacy policy at any time. Your continued use
      of this site after any change in this privacy policy will constitute your acceptance of such
      change.
    </p>

  </div>
</section>
</Base>
